    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Represents static data in an executable.</para><para>For now, we don&apos;t associate any type with the data because ROSE&apos;s data type infrastructure (source or binary) is not capable of representing the information we need: multiple interpretations of overlapping parts of memory (i.e., two or more types for the same bytes); arbitrary offsets and padding in structured types; size-specific integers and floating-point types; regions of unknown type; ease of improving type information by filling in more details as the type is discovered; etc. </para>    </detaileddescription>
